WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.609
Wherever a connector action exists, the
ticket should authorize the machine,

2
00:00:04.609 --> 00:00:06.888
and the person's role stops at approval.

3
00:00:06.888 --> 00:00:09.288
But check what the
connector really documents.

4
00:00:09.288 --> 00:00:12.287
The book checked ServiceNow's
Entra ID spoke and

5
00:00:12.287 --> 00:00:15.212
found the older design
had mapped too much to it.

6
00:00:15.212 --> 00:00:18.876
Its password reset works
only for cloud-only users.

7
00:00:18.876 --> 00:00:23.343
There's no action at all for an MFA
reset, so that stays a person's task,

8
00:00:23.343 --> 00:00:27.162
which makes verification the
control that matters most.

9
00:00:27.162 --> 00:00:30.400
And the connection type decides
which actions run at all,

10
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.775
because some of them work only
with delegated permissions.

11
00:00:33.775 --> 00:00:38.050
Coverage changes by release, so validate
it against what you've installed.

12
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:40.320
Which brings us to verifying the person.
